#
Network Isolation (Virtual Networks) Documentation

By default, standard public deployments expose the application login screen to the global web, making it vulnerable to automated brute-force or credential-stuffing attacks. To satisfy enterprise cybersecurity standards, this system must utilize Network Isolation to restrict dashboard visibility solely to internal authorized corporate boundaries.
#
1. Network Topology Model Enabling network isolation encapsulates both your dynamic application instance container and database layer deep within an isolated, private virtual runtime bubble [13].
#
[ Public Web Space ]
         │
         ▼ (Public Inbound Requests Blocked ❌)
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  🔒 Enterprise Private Space Perimeter                 │
│                                                        │
│  ┌────────────────────────┐    ┌────────────────────┐  │
│  │ Corporate VPN Gateway  │───>│ Dashboard App      │  │
│  │ (Authorized Inbound)   │    │ (Docker Service)   │  │
│  └────────────────────────┘    └─────────┬──────────┘  │
│                                          │             │
│                                          ▼             │
│                                ┌────────────────────┐  │
│                                │ Internal Databases │  │
│                                └────────────────────┘  │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
 2. Structural Infrastructure-as-Code Configuration To establish this secure enterprise perimeter programmatically, future cloud administrators must configure the orchestration environment blueprint directly inside the root render.yaml specification file [13].Replace or wrap your current execution parameters using the strict group cluster schema below:

# =============================================================
# Render Private Space Project Specification
# =============================================================
projects:
  - name: enterprise-finops-suite
    environments:
      - name: corporate-production
        
        # 1. Activate strict private cloud firewall parameters
        networking:
          isolation: enabled # ◄── Drops all unauthenticated public internet traffic [13]
        
        # 2. Bind the dockerized cost utility into the isolated workspace
        services:
          - type: web
            name: azure-cost-dashboard
            runtime: docker
            dockerfilePath: ./Dockerfile
            plan: free
            healthCheckPath: /api/health
            envVars:
              - key: NODE_ENV
                value: production
